// draft, and once paid anything the server refuses further changes. A sent invoice takes payments
// until nothing is due, less than $1.00 left being written off; the panel lists them with what has
// been paid, what is still due and what was written off. The
// server refuses a payment on a draft, over what is due, or dated after today or before the issue date.
// The panel shows the invoice's RF payment reference; a payment may quote one, which must pass the

// Records a payment. With no parts filled in it goes to the open invoice (`invoiceId`), or, when none
// is open, to the client's invoices whose references are quoted (several may be, separated by
// commas: RF references or invoice numbers, applied earliest due date first), or without one to the client's unpaid invoices earliest due date first; once any invoice in the list has a part, the
// payment is spread over those invoices instead, and the parts must add up to it. The server refuses a payment on a draft, over what is due, or dated after today
// or before the issue date; a quoted reference must pass the ISO 11649 check and be the invoice's. The
// invoice number may be quoted instead: it must pass its Luhn check and stands for that invoice's reference.
  }

  // Records a payment against a sent invoice that still has something due; refused (409) when it
  // is a draft, already paid, the amount is more than is due, or the date is after today or before
  // the issue date, or the reference is mistyped (400) or another invoice's (409). Answers the invoice with its payments and new status.
  recordPayment(invoiceId: number, payment: NewPayment): Observable<InvoiceDetail> {
    return this.http.post<InvoiceDetail>(`/api/invoices/${invoiceId}/payments`, payment);
  }

  // Records one payment spread over several of the client's invoices; refused (409) unless the parts
  // add up to the payment and each goes to a sent invoice of the client, no more than it has due.
  // With no parts it goes to the invoices whose references are quoted (comma separated), earliest due
  // date first, refused when one is mistyped (400), not the client's, or they owe less than the payment.
  // Answers the client's invoices with their new statuses.

